{"artifact_id":"extract_4fe2ad4c9b61509644b70c23","byte_end":58799,"byte_start":57286,"format_id":"reviewed-html-paragraph-v1","locator":"Ch0.S3.p7.1","original_html":"<p id=\"Ch0.S3.p7.1\" class=\"ltx_p\">The production of SBs depends on two parameters, the string scale <math id=\"Ch0.S3.p7.m1\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"M_{\\text{S}}\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mtext>S</mtext></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">M_{\\text{S}}</annotation></semantics></math> and the string coupling <math id=\"Ch0.S3.p7.m2\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"g_{\\text{S}}\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mtext>S</mtext></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">g_{\\text{S}}</annotation></semantics></math>. For all SB samples, <math id=\"Ch0.S3.p7.m3\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"n=6\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n=6</annotation></semantics></math> is used.\nIn weakly-coupled string scenarios compactified to <math id=\"Ch0.S3.p7.m4\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"4+n\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">4+n</annotation></semantics></math> dimensions, <math id=\"Ch0.S3.p7.m5\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"M_{\\text{D}}\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mtext>D</mtext></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">M_{\\text{D}}</annotation></semantics></math> and the string parameters are related by <cite class=\"ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite\">[<a href=\"#bib.bib48\" title=\"\" class=\"ltx_ref\">48</a>]</cite>,</p>","parser_version":"1.0.0","purpose":"RESEARCH","review_status":"PROPOSED","schema_version":"1.0.0","source_hash":"7fadcfce5fce60055ccd817d98d05c9d09e4c759f1691022a0d3f4f7cf2be955","source_id":"cms_paper_v2","source_version":"2604.10732v2"}